  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5524",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a potential target for MDA-MB-415 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with A704, which in turn is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this compound further targets MDA-MB-415. Similarly, Mollicellin N is also linked to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that ultimately affects MDA-MB-415. Additionally, Mollicellin N is associated with TE-9, which is also targeted by the same compound that influences MDA-MB-415. These pathways collectively indicate that Mollicellin N may modulate MDA-MB-415 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by interacting with receptors or signaling pathways that are downstream of the compound it targets. The integration of these evidence points highlights a potential role for Mollicellin N in influencing MDA-MB-415 through a network of targets, suggesting a complex, multi-tiered interaction that may be relevant in therapeutic contexts.",
